+    are an integer array with one ``[start, stop]`` row per dimension, channel included, in the original unpadded
+    image. For example, a single-channel 2D image gives patches of shape (1, 2, 2) and coordinates of shape (3, 2).
+
+    For example, to sample 2x2 patches from single-channel 4x4 images with a per-patch intensity shift:
+
